  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 136 PM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nThe upper-level ridge axis shifts farther to our west by Saturday, \nyielding highs 3 to 5 degrees cooler than Friday's. However, triple \ndigit temperatures become confined to the river valleys, with mid-to-\nupper 90s elsewhere. Meanwhile, we cannot rule out the chance of an \nisolated shower/storm or two across portions of southeast New Mexico \nand higher terrain (thanks to southeasterly upslope flow) Saturday \nafternoon as a surface lee cyclone passes just to our north. Sunday \nand beyond, the upper-level ridge strengthens aloft and heights \nincrease across the region. This allows for widespread triple digit \nhighs to return, with the hottest spots along the river valleys once \nagain. Some locations along the Pecos River look to see readings \nnear 105 degrees through at least the middle of next week. Whereas \nfolks along the Rio Grande could see readings top out between 105 \nand 110 degrees, especially in low-lying areas. Be sure to drink \nplenty of fluids and take frequent breaks under shade if you must be \noutside for an extended period of time!\n  \nGreening",
